IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mai-dates`

-- Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 (Qld) -- the claims machinery of Part 4, seat-neutral core.
--
-- In the Act's own actors and terms: "the claimant", "the insurer", "the Nominal Defendant", "the supervising
-- principal" of a law practice, "the court". The claimant's questions are in mai-seat.l4; this module holds the rules.
--
-- Edition: Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 (act-1994-009), current in-force version on 22 September 2026, as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/act-1994-009.txt. The Motor Accident Insurance Regulation 2018 (the
-- contents of the notice of claim, the documents with it) is not deposited; the offer limits and the declared costs
-- limit are fixed by the Minister under s 100A and are not deposited either. The period of limitation is set by the
-- Limitation of Actions Act 1974, not deposited. Each is asked as a fact.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Part 4 -- Claims (Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994, Qld)`

§§ `s 4 -- claim, claimant, motor vehicle accident`

-- s 4: "motor vehicle accident means an incident from which a liability for personal injury arises that is covered
-- by insurance under the statutory insurance scheme." The statutory insurance scheme (CTP insurance, and the Nominal
-- Defendant for uninsured and unidentified vehicles) is asked as a fact. "Personal injury includes ..." is asked as a
-- fact too.
GIVEN `a liability for personal injury arises from the incident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability is covered by insurance under the statutory insurance scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the incident is a motor vehicle accident` `a liability for personal injury arises from the incident` `the liability is covered by insurance under the statutory insurance scheme` IF
        `a liability for personal injury arises from the incident`
    AND `the liability is covered by insurance under the statutory insurance scheme`

-- Who the person is, in relation to the injury.
DECLARE `Standing` IS ONE OF
    `the injured person`
    `a person acting for the injured person in a representative capacity`
    `a dependant of an injured person who died of the injury`
    `the personal representative of the estate of an injured person who died of the injury`
    `someone else`

-- s 4: "claim means a claim for damages based on a liability for personal injury arising out of a motor vehicle
-- accident and, for a fatal injury, includes a claim on behalf of the deceased's dependants or estate." "claimant means
-- a person by whom, or on whose behalf, a claim is made." Examples 1 and 2: an attorney, guardian or administrator
-- (in that capacity) and the injured person are both claimants.
-- JUST FALSE where there is no motor vehicle accident ("means"). For someone else, NOTHING: the definition of claim
-- "includes" the fatal-injury claims without closing the list, and a person injured in their own right (for example
-- by shock) is "the injured person".
GIVEN `the incident is a motor vehicle accident (s 4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `standing`                                     IS A `Standing`
      `damages are claimed`                          IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is a claimant (s 4)` `the incident is a motor vehicle accident (s 4)` `standing` `damages are claimed` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the incident is a motor vehicle accident (s 4)` AND `damages are claimed`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `standing`
         WHEN `the injured person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a person acting for the injured person in a representative capacity` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a dependant of an injured person who died of the injury` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `the personal representative of the estate of an injured person who died of the injury` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `someone else` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Division 1 -- the insurer (ss 31, 33)`

DECLARE `The insurer` IS ONE OF
    `the insurer under the vehicle's CTP insurance policy`
    `the self-insurer that is the vehicle's registered owner`
    `the Nominal Defendant`

DECLARE `Insurer answer` IS ONE OF
    `the insurer is` HAS `who` IS A `The insurer`
    `the Nominal Defendant is not liable for this accident outside Queensland (s 33(3))`

-- s 31(1): "(a) if the motor vehicle is an insured motor vehicle--the insurer under the CTP insurance policy is ... the
-- insurer; (b) if the motor vehicle is not insured but a self-insurer is the registered owner--the self-insurer is the
-- insurer; (c) if the motor vehicle is not insured and a self-insurer is not the registered owner--the Nominal
-- Defendant is the insurer; (d) if the motor vehicle, or insurer under its CTP insurance policy, can not be
-- identified--the Nominal Defendant is the insurer."
-- s 33(2): if the CTP insurer becomes insolvent, the Nominal Defendant becomes the insurer "unless the policies are
-- transferred to some other licensed insurer" (that insurer is then the insurer under the policy: the first branch).
-- s 33(3): "The Nominal Defendant is liable for personal injury arising out of a motor vehicle accident outside
-- Queensland only if-- (a) the liability arises under subsection (2); or (b) ... a motor vehicle that is gratuitously
-- insured under section 23(7)."
-- Trailers (s 31(3)-(4)) are out of scope.
GIVEN `the vehicle can be identified`                     IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vehicle is insured under a CTP insurance policy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the CTP insurer can be identified`                 IS A BOOLEAN
      `the CTP insurer is insolvent and the policy was not transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a self-insurer is the registered owner`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accident happened outside Queensland`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vehicle is gratuitously insured under s 23(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Insurer answer`
`the insurer under ss 31 and 33` `the vehicle can be identified` `the vehicle is insured under a CTP insurance policy` `the CTP insurer can be identified` `the CTP insurer is insolvent and the policy was not transferred` `a self-insurer is the registered owner` `the accident happened outside Queensland` `the vehicle is gratuitously insured under s 23(7)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the vehicle can be identified`
    THEN `the Nominal Defendant, outside Queensland only under s 33(3)` FALSE
    ELSE IF `the vehicle is insured under a CTP insurance policy`
         THEN IF NOT `the CTP insurer can be identified`
              THEN `the Nominal Defendant, outside Queensland only under s 33(3)` FALSE
              ELSE IF `the CTP insurer is insolvent and the policy was not transferred`
                   THEN `the Nominal Defendant, outside Queensland only under s 33(3)` TRUE
                   ELSE `the insurer is` `the insurer under the vehicle's CTP insurance policy`
         ELSE IF `a self-insurer is the registered owner`
              THEN `the insurer is` `the self-insurer that is the vehicle's registered owner`
              ELSE `the Nominal Defendant, outside Queensland only under s 33(3)` FALSE
    WHERE
        `the Nominal Defendant, outside Queensland only under s 33(3)` `by insolvency` MEANS
            IF     `the accident happened outside Queensland`
               AND NOT (`by insolvency` OR `the vehicle is gratuitously insured under s 23(7)`)
            THEN `the Nominal Defendant is not liable for this accident outside Queensland (s 33(3))`
            ELSE `the insurer is` `the Nominal Defendant`

§§ `Division 2 -- s 34 notice of the accident to police`

DECLARE `Police notice answer` IS ONE OF
    `no duty under s 34: no claim is proposed`
    `appropriate notice has been given: the particulars required under the Transport Operations (Road Use Management) Act 1995 s 93(4) were given`
    `the claimant must ensure a police officer is given notice under s 34, in the form approved by the commission`

-- s 34(1): "A person who proposes to make a claim (including a person acting in a representative capacity) must ensure
-- that appropriate notice of the accident has been given to a police officer." (2) "Appropriate notice ... is-- (a)
-- the giving of required particulars under the Transport Operations (Road Use Management) Act 1995, section 93(4); or
-- (b) if (and only if) particulars have not been given as required under that section--a notice under this section in
-- a form approved by the commission." s 34 sets no time.
GIVEN `a claim is proposed`                         IS A BOOLEAN
      `the TORUM s 93(4) particulars have been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Police notice answer`
`the s 34 answer` `a claim is proposed` `the TORUM s 93(4) particulars have been given` MEANS
    IF NOT `a claim is proposed`
    THEN `no duty under s 34: no claim is proposed`
    ELSE IF `the TORUM s 93(4) particulars have been given`
         THEN `appropriate notice has been given: the particulars required under the Transport Operations (Road Use Management) Act 1995 s 93(4) were given`
         ELSE `the claimant must ensure a police officer is given notice under s 34, in the form approved by the commission`

§§ `Division 3 -- s 37 notice of accident claim, with s 40`

-- The facts that fix the s 37(2) period.
DECLARE `Notice facts` HAS
    `the day of the accident`                                 IS A DATE
    `the vehicle can be identified`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `symptoms were immediately apparent`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day symptoms first appeared`                         IS A DATE
    `a lawyer has been consulted about a possible claim`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day a lawyer was first consulted`                    IS A DATE
    `the obligation was suspended by minority or incapacity`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the minority or incapacity ended`                IS A DATE

-- s 40(1)-(2): "A claimant's obligation to comply with this division is suspended during the claimant's minority or a
-- period of legal incapacity. A period within which the obligation is to be complied with begins when the claimant's
-- minority or legal incapacity ends."
-- READING (finding 2): each period of s 37 that would begin earlier begins instead on the day the minority or
-- incapacity ends; one that begins later (symptoms, or a lawyer, after that day) is unchanged.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Notice facts`
      `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the start of a period under s 40` `the facts` `the start` MEANS
    IF `the facts`'s `the obligation was suspended by minority or incapacity`
    THEN `the later of` `the start` `and` (`the facts`'s `the day the minority or incapacity ended`)
    ELSE `the start`

-- s 37(2): "The notice must be given-- (a) if it is to be given to the Nominal Defendant because the motor vehicle can
-- not be identified--within 3 months after the motor vehicle accident; or (b) in any other case--within the period
-- ending on the earlier of the following dates-- (i) 9 months after the motor vehicle accident or, if symptoms of the
-- injury are not immediately apparent, the first appearance of symptoms of the injury; (ii) 1 month after the claimant
-- first consults a lawyer about the possibility of making a claim."
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Notice facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the s 37(2) period` `the facts` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the facts`'s `the vehicle can be identified`)
    THEN `the day` 3 `months after` (`the start of a period under s 40` `the facts` (`the facts`'s `the day of the accident`))
    ELSE IF `the facts`'s `a lawyer has been consulted about a possible claim`
         THEN `the earlier of` `nine months` `and` `one month after the lawyer`
         ELSE `nine months`
    WHERE
        `nine months` MEANS
            IF `the facts`'s `symptoms were immediately apparent`
            THEN `the day` 9 `months after` (`the start of a period under s 40` `the facts` (`the facts`'s `the day of the accident`))
            ELSE `the day` 9 `months after` (`the start of a period under s 40` `the facts` (`the facts`'s `the day symptoms first appeared`))
        `one month after the lawyer` MEANS
            `the day` 1 `months after` (`the start of a period under s 40` `the facts` (`the facts`'s `the day a lawyer was first consulted`))

-- s 37(3): "... if a motor vehicle can not be identified and the notice is not given to the Nominal Defendant within 9
-- months after the motor vehicle accident, the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred."
-- READING (finding 2): the 9 months are a period within which the obligation is to be complied with, so s 40(2) moves
-- their start too.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Notice facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day before the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred` `the facts` MEANS
    `the day` 9 `months after` (`the start of a period under s 40` `the facts` (`the facts`'s `the day of the accident`))

GIVEN `the facts`                IS A `Notice facts`
      `notice has been given`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about`      IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred under s 37(3)` `the facts` `notice has been given` `the day notice was given` `the day asked about` IF
        NOT (`the facts`'s `the vehicle can be identified`)
    AND `the day asked about` `is after` (`the last day before the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred` `the facts`)
    AND NOT (    `notice has been given`
             AND `the day notice was given` `is no later than` (`the last day before the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred` `the facts`))

DECLARE `Notice answer` IS ONE OF
    `notice of the claim must be given by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `notice was given within the s 37(2) period`
    `notice is late: it must still be given, with a reasonable excuse for the delay (s 37(3))` HAS `the period ended on` IS A DATE
    `the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred: no notice within 9 months (ss 37(3), 39(8))` HAS `the 9 months ended on` IS A DATE

-- s 40(3): notice given during the minority or incapacity, before the period begins, is in time.
GIVEN `the facts`                IS A `Notice facts`
      `notice has been given`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about`      IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
`the s 37 answer` `the facts` `notice has been given` `the day notice was given` `the day asked about` MEANS
    IF `the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred under s 37(3)` `the facts` `notice has been given` `the day notice was given` `the day asked about`
    THEN `the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred: no notice within 9 months (ss 37(3), 39(8))` (`the last day before the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred` `the facts`)
    ELSE IF `notice has been given`
         THEN IF `the day notice was given` `is no later than` (`the last day of the s 37(2) period` `the facts`)
              THEN `notice was given within the s 37(2) period`
              ELSE `notice is late: it must still be given, with a reasonable excuse for the delay (s 37(3))` (`the last day of the s 37(2) period` `the facts`)
         ELSE IF `the day asked about` `is no later than` (`the last day of the s 37(2) period` `the facts`)
              THEN `notice of the claim must be given by` (`the last day of the s 37(2) period` `the facts`)
              ELSE `notice is late: it must still be given, with a reasonable excuse for the delay (s 37(3))` (`the last day of the s 37(2) period` `the facts`)

-- s 57(3): "If during the last 14 days of the period of limitation, the claimant wants to give a notice of claim under
-- division 3 but is unsure to which insurer the notice should be given, the notice is validly given if it is given to
-- the commission." READING: the last 14 days are the last day of the period and the 13 days before it.
GIVEN `the last day of the period of limitation` IS A DATE
      `the day of giving notice`                 IS A DATE
      `the claimant is unsure which insurer`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `notice may validly be given to the commission (s 57(3))` `the last day of the period of limitation` `the day of giving notice` `the claimant is unsure which insurer` IF
        `the claimant is unsure which insurer`
    AND `the day of giving notice` `is no later than` `the last day of the period of limitation`
    AND `the first of the last 14 days` `is no later than` `the day of giving notice`
    WHERE
        `the first of the last 14 days` MEANS `the day` 13 `days before` `the last day of the period of limitation`

§§ `Division 3 -- s 37AA refund, s 37A additional information, s 39 response, s 41 resolution`

DECLARE `Refund answer` IS ONE OF
    `the supervising principal must refund all fees and costs, including disbursements, by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `s 37AA gives no refund on these facts`

-- s 37AA: "(1) ... if-- (a) the supervising principal of a law practice ... fails to give a law practice certificate to
-- the claimant as required under section 36A; and (b) because of the principal's failure, the claimant-- (i) cannot
-- comply with the requirements of section 37(1) within the period mentioned in section 37(2); and (ii) terminates in
-- writing the engagement of the law practice ... (2) The principal must, within 14 days after the termination, refund
-- to the claimant all fees and costs, including disbursements, paid by the claimant in relation to the claim."
GIVEN `the principal failed to give the s 36A certificate`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `because of it the claimant cannot give notice within the s 37(2) period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant terminated the engagement in writing`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of termination`                                      IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Refund answer`
`the s 37AA answer` `the principal failed to give the s 36A certificate` `because of it the claimant cannot give notice within the s 37(2) period` `the claimant terminated the engagement in writing` `the day of termination` MEANS
    IF     `the principal failed to give the s 36A certificate`
       AND `because of it the claimant cannot give notice within the s 37(2) period`
       AND `the claimant terminated the engagement in writing`
    THEN `the supervising principal must refund all fees and costs, including disbursements, by` (`the day` 14 `days after` `the day of termination`)
    ELSE `s 37AA gives no refund on these facts`

-- s 37A(3): "The claimant must, within 1 month after the date of the request, provide the information to the insurer
-- in a form approved by the commission (an additional information form)."
GIVEN `the day of the request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the additional information form (s 37A(3))` `the day of the request` MEANS
    `the day` 1 `months after` `the day of the request`

DECLARE `Response answer` IS ONE OF
    `the insurer must respond by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the insurer responded in time; what follows depends on its response (s 39(1))`
    `the insurer is conclusively presumed satisfied that the notice was given as required (s 39(3))` HAS `the 14 days ended on` IS A DATE

-- s 39(1)(a): "the insurer must, within 14 days after receiving the notice give the claimant written notice-- (i)
-- stating whether the insurer is satisfied that the notice has been given as required ..." (3): "If ... the insurer
-- does not respond to the notice within 14 days after receiving it, the insurer is conclusively presumed to be
-- satisfied the notice was given as required under this division." (4): the insurer may still later deny it is the
-- insurer of the vehicle.
GIVEN `the day the insurer received the notice` IS A DATE
      `the insurer has responded`               IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the insurer responded`           IS A DATE
      `the day asked about`                     IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Response answer`
`the s 39 answer` `the day the insurer received the notice` `the insurer has responded` `the day the insurer responded` `the day asked about` MEANS
    IF `the insurer has responded` AND `the day the insurer responded` `is no later than` `the last day`
    THEN `the insurer responded in time; what follows depends on its response (s 39(1))`
    ELSE IF `the day asked about` `is no later than` `the last day`
         THEN `the insurer must respond by` `the last day`
         ELSE `the insurer is conclusively presumed satisfied that the notice was given as required (s 39(3))` `the last day`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `the day` 14 `days after` `the day the insurer received the notice`

DECLARE `Proceed answer` IS ONE OF
    `the claimant may proceed further with the claim`
    `the claimant may not proceed further: notice was not given as required, and none of s 39(5)(a) to (c) applies`
    `the claimant may not proceed: the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred, and it cannot waive nor the court give leave (ss 37(3), 39(8))`

-- s 39(5): "A claimant's failure to give notice of a claim as required under this division prevents the claimant from
-- proceeding further with the claim unless-- (a) the insurer-- (i) has stated that the insurer is satisfied notice has
-- been given as required ... or the claimant has taken reasonable action to remedy the noncompliance; or (ii) is
-- presumed to be satisfied ...; or (b) the insurer has waived compliance with the requirement; or (c) the court, on
-- application by the claimant-- (i) declares that the claimant has remedied the noncompliance; or (ii) authorises
-- further proceedings based on the claim despite the noncompliance."
-- s 39(8): for a claim barred under s 37(3), "the Nominal Defendant can not waive compliance ... nor can the court give
-- leave". READING (finding 4): the s 37(3) bar stands whatever the insurer says or is presumed to say.
GIVEN `the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice was given as required`                              IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insurer stated it is satisfied`                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insurer is presumed satisfied`                         IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insurer waived compliance`                             IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court declared the noncompliance remedied or authorised further proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Proceed answer`
`the s 39(5) answer` `the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred` `notice was given as required` `the insurer stated it is satisfied` `the insurer is presumed satisfied` `the insurer waived compliance` `the court declared the noncompliance remedied or authorised further proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred`
    THEN `the claimant may not proceed: the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred, and it cannot waive nor the court give leave (ss 37(3), 39(8))`
    ELSE IF    `notice was given as required`
            OR `the insurer stated it is satisfied`
            OR `the insurer is presumed satisfied`
            OR `the insurer waived compliance`
            OR `the court declared the noncompliance remedied or authorised further proceedings`
         THEN `the claimant may proceed further with the claim`
         ELSE `the claimant may not proceed further: notice was not given as required, and none of s 39(5)(a) to (c) applies`

DECLARE `Liability notice answer` IS ONE OF
    `the insurer must say whether it admits or denies liability by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the 6 months have not started: the notice is not yet taken to be received (s 41(3))`

-- s 41(1): "Within 6 months after an insurer receives notice of a claim under this division, the insurer must-- ... (b)
-- give the claimant written notice stating-- (i) whether liability is admitted or denied; and (ii) if contributory
-- negligence is claimed--the degree ... as a percentage ..." (3): "If a notice of claim is not given as required ...
-- the insurer is taken to receive the notice when-- (a) the insurer gives the claimant notice that the insurer waives
-- compliance ... or is satisfied the claimant has taken reasonable action to remedy the noncompliance; or (b) the
-- court makes a declaration ... or gives leave ..."
-- READING (finding 5): a notice the insurer is presumed under s 39(3) to accept was "given as required", so it is
-- received on the day it arrived.
GIVEN `notice was given as required or is presumed to be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the insurer received the notice`           IS A DATE
      `there has been a waiver, satisfaction notice or court order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the waiver, satisfaction notice or court order`   IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Liability notice answer`
`the s 41 answer` `notice was given as required or is presumed to be` `the day the insurer received the notice` `there has been a waiver, satisfaction notice or court order` `the day of the waiver, satisfaction notice or court order` MEANS
    IF `notice was given as required or is presumed to be`
    THEN `the insurer must say whether it admits or denies liability by` (`the day` 6 `months after` `the day the insurer received the notice`)
    ELSE IF `there has been a waiver, satisfaction notice or court order`
         THEN `the insurer must say whether it admits or denies liability by` (`the day` 6 `months after` `the day of the waiver, satisfaction notice or court order`)
         ELSE `the 6 months have not started: the notice is not yet taken to be received (s 41(3))`

-- s 41(5): "An insurer or claimant to whom a written offer (or counter offer) of settlement is made must ... respond in
-- writing to the offer, within 3 months after receiving it, indicating acceptance or rejection of the offer."
GIVEN `the day the offer was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to respond to an offer (s 41(5))` `the day the offer was received` MEANS
    `the day` 3 `months after` `the day the offer was received`

§§ `Division 3 -- s 42 private hospital, medical and pharmaceutical expenses`

DECLARE `Expenses answer` IS ONE OF
    `the insurer must pay, in Australian dollars,` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no duty yet: liability has not been admitted (s 42(1))`
    `the insurer need not pay for treatment, care and support needs (s 42(3))`

-- s 42(1): "Once liability has been admitted, it is the duty of the insurer to make payments to or for the claimant for
-- private hospital, medical and pharmaceutical expenses reasonably and appropriately incurred because of the injury
-- or a proportionate part of the expenses reflecting the extent of the insurer's responsibility (assuming the claimant
-- to be guilty of contributory negligence as asserted by the insurer)." (3): not for treatment, care and support needs
-- that arise while the claimant is a participant in the injury insurance scheme, or after a National Injury Act
-- s 44(3)(a) payment. "Reasonably and appropriately incurred" is the claimant's figure, taken as such.
GIVEN `liability has been admitted`                 IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expenses`                                IS A NUMBER
      `the contributory negligence asserted, percent` IS A NUMBER
      `the needs arose while a participant in the injury insurance scheme, or after a National Injury Act s 44(3)(a) payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Expenses answer`
`the s 42 answer` `liability has been admitted` `the expenses` `the contributory negligence asserted, percent` `the needs arose while a participant in the injury insurance scheme, or after a National Injury Act s 44(3)(a) payment` MEANS
    IF NOT `liability has been admitted`
    THEN `no duty yet: liability has not been admitted (s 42(1))`
    ELSE IF `the needs arose while a participant in the injury insurance scheme, or after a National Injury Act s 44(3)(a) payment`
         THEN `the insurer need not pay for treatment, care and support needs (s 42(3))`
         ELSE `the insurer must pay, in Australian dollars,` (`reduce` `the expenses` `by percent` `the contributory negligence asserted, percent`)

§§ `Division 4 -- ss 45 and 47 cooperation`

DECLARE `Claimant cooperation step` IS ONE OF
    `give copies of reports and documents I hold when I give notice`
    `give copies of reports and documents that come into my possession later`
    `answer the insurer's request for information`
    `tell the insurer of a significant change in my condition or circumstances`

-- s 45(2): "The claimant must-- (a) provide the copies of reports and other documentary materials within 1 month after
-- giving notice of the claim or, if the reports or material come into the claimant's possession later, within 1
-- month after they come into the claimant's possession; and (b) respond to a request under subsection (1)(b) within 1
-- month after receiving it." (3): a significant change, after notice and before the claim is resolved, "within 1
-- month after becoming aware of the change". Every step is 1 month after the day that starts it.
GIVEN `the step`                    IS A `Claimant cooperation step`
      `the day that starts the step` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the claimant's step (s 45)` `the step` `the day that starts the step` MEANS
    `the day` 1 `months after` `the day that starts the step`

-- s 47(2): the insurer must "(a) provide the claimant with copies of reports and other documentary materials within 1
-- month after receiving the notice of claim ... or, if the reports or materials come into the insurer's possession
-- later, within 1 month after they come into the insurer's possession; and (b) respond to a request under subsection
-- (1)(b) within 1 month after receiving it." (4): an insurer that fails without proper reason is liable for the
-- claimant's resulting costs.
GIVEN `the day that starts the insurer's step` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the insurer's step (s 47)` `the day that starts the insurer's step` MEANS
    `the day` 1 `months after` `the day that starts the insurer's step`

§§ `Division 5 -- s 51(9)-(9A) rehabilitation costs in damages`

-- s 51(9): the insurer's cost of rehabilitation services is taken into account in the assessment of damages "if (and
-- only if) the insurer gave a statement to the claimant, as required under subsection (4) ...". (9A): "(a) the
-- claimant's damages are first assessed (without reduction for contributory negligence) on the assumption that the
-- claimant has incurred the cost of the rehabilitation services ...; (b) any reduction ... on account of contributory
-- negligence is then made; (c) the total cost of rehabilitation services is then set-off against the amount assessed."
-- Without the statement, the damages are reduced for contributory negligence and nothing is set off. The result is
-- not floored at nil (finding 7).
GIVEN `the damages before contributory negligence, without rehabilitation` IS A NUMBER
      `the insurer's cost of rehabilitation services` IS A NUMBER
      `contributory negligence, percent`              IS A NUMBER
      `the insurer gave the s 51(4) statement`        IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the damages after s 51(9A)` `the damages before contributory negligence, without rehabilitation` `the insurer's cost of rehabilitation services` `contributory negligence, percent` `the insurer gave the s 51(4) statement` MEANS
    IF `the insurer gave the s 51(4) statement`
    THEN (`reduce` (`the damages before contributory negligence, without rehabilitation` PLUS `the insurer's cost of rehabilitation services`) `by percent` `contributory negligence, percent`) MINUS `the insurer's cost of rehabilitation services`
    ELSE `reduce` `the damages before contributory negligence, without rehabilitation` `by percent` `contributory negligence, percent`

§§ `Division 5A -- compulsory conference and mandatory final offers (ss 51A-51D)`

-- s 51A(3): "the relevant date is-- (a) the date falling 6 months after the claimant gave notice to the insurer of the
-- claim; or (b) if the insurer required additional information, the later of the following-- (i) the date falling 6
-- months after the claimant gave notice ...; (ii) the date falling 1 month after the claimant gave the insurer the
-- completed additional information form." (2)(b): once the relevant date "has passed", either party may call the
-- conference at a reasonable time and place it nominates.
GIVEN `the day notice of the claim was given`                IS A DATE
      `the insurer required additional information`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the additional information form was given`    IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the relevant date (s 51A(3))` `the day notice of the claim was given` `the insurer required additional information` `the day the additional information form was given` MEANS
    IF `the insurer required additional information`
    THEN `the later of` (`the day` 6 `months after` `the day notice of the claim was given`) `and` (`the day` 1 `months after` `the day the additional information form was given`)
    ELSE `the day` 6 `months after` `the day notice of the claim was given`

-- s 51B(5): "At least 7 days before the compulsory conference is held, each party must give the other party-- (a)
-- copies of all documents not yet given ...; (b) a statement verifying ...; (c) details of the party's legal
-- representation; and (d) if the party has legal representation--a certificate of readiness ..."
GIVEN `the day of the conference` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the s 51B(5) documents` `the day of the conference` MEANS
    `the day` 7 `days before` `the day of the conference`

-- s 51C(1)(b): where the conference is dispensed with, mandatory final offers are exchanged "within 14 days after the
-- date of the agreement or order dispensing with the conference".
GIVEN `the day of the agreement or order dispensing with the conference` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to exchange mandatory final offers (s 51C(1)(b))` `the day of the agreement or order dispensing with the conference` MEANS
    `the day` 14 `days after` `the day of the agreement or order dispensing with the conference`

-- s 51C(6): "A mandatory final offer must remain open for 14 days and proceedings must not be started while the offer
-- remains open." READING (finding 8): the 14 days are the 14 days after the day the offers were exchanged, so
-- proceedings may be started from the 15th day after it.
GIVEN `the day the mandatory final offers were exchanged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day proceedings may be started after the offers (s 51C(6))` `the day the mandatory final offers were exchanged` MEANS
    `the day` 15 `days after` `the day the mandatory final offers were exchanged`

DECLARE `Start answer` IS ONE OF
    `the action should be started by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the action should be started within the period the court fixed when dispensing with mandatory final offers (s 51D(3))`

-- s 51D(1): "An action for damages should be started in the court-- (a) within 60 days after the conclusion of the
-- compulsory conference; or (b) within a further period-- (i) agreed by the parties within the 60 day period ...; or
-- (ii) fixed by the court on an application made by the claimant within the 60 day period ..."
-- (2): if the conference is dispensed with, "(a) within 60 days after the later of the following-- (i) the date
-- falling 6 months after the date on which the claimant gives notice to the insurer of the claim or if the insurer
-- asks for additional information, the date on which the claimant gives the insurer the completed additional
-- information form; (ii) the date of the agreement or order dispensing with the conference; or (b) within a further
-- period ..." READING (finding 9): (2)(a)(i) taken as written: where additional information was asked for, the date is
-- the day the form was given, not the later of that and 6 months after notice.
-- (3): if the court dispenses with mandatory final offers, "within a period fixed by the court".
GIVEN `the conference was dispensed with`                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the conference concluded`                         IS A DATE
      `the day notice of the claim was given`                    IS A DATE
      `the insurer asked for additional information`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the additional information form was given`        IS A DATE
      `the day of the agreement or order dispensing with the conference` IS A DATE
      `a further period was agreed or fixed within the 60 days`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the further period`                       IS A DATE
      `the court dispensed with mandatory final offers`          IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Start answer`
`the s 51D answer` `the conference was dispensed with` `the day the conference concluded` `the day notice of the claim was given` `the insurer asked for additional information` `the day the additional information form was given` `the day of the agreement or order dispensing with the conference` `a further period was agreed or fixed within the 60 days` `the last day of the further period` `the court dispensed with mandatory final offers` MEANS
    IF `the court dispensed with mandatory final offers`
    THEN `the action should be started within the period the court fixed when dispensing with mandatory final offers (s 51D(3))`
    ELSE IF `a further period was agreed or fixed within the 60 days`
         THEN `the action should be started by` `the last day of the further period`
         ELSE IF `the conference was dispensed with`
              THEN `the action should be started by` (`the day` 60 `days after` (`the later of` `the s 51D(2)(a)(i) date` `and` `the day of the agreement or order dispensing with the conference`))
              ELSE `the action should be started by` (`the day` 60 `days after` `the day the conference concluded`)
    WHERE
        `the s 51D(2)(a)(i) date` MEANS
            IF `the insurer asked for additional information`
            THEN `the day the additional information form was given`
            ELSE `the day` 6 `months after` `the day notice of the claim was given`

-- s 51D(4): "The expiry of the time within which an action should be started ... does not prevent the claimant from
-- starting the action but-- (a) the court may (unless the claimant establishes a reasonable excuse for the delay)
-- order the claimant to pay ... the insurer's costs arising out of the delay; and (b) the court may, on the insurer's
-- application, make an order fixing a time limit within which the action must be started." (5): "If the claimant fails
-- to start an action in the court within a time limit fixed under subsection (4)(b), the claim is barred."
GIVEN `the court fixed a time limit under s 51D(4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of that time limit`              IS A DATE
      `the action has been started`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the action was started`               IS A DATE
      `the day asked about`                          IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is barred under s 51D(5)` `the court fixed a time limit under s 51D(4)(b)` `the last day of that time limit` `the action has been started` `the day the action was started` `the day asked about` IF
        `the court fixed a time limit under s 51D(4)(b)`
    AND `the day asked about` `is after` `the last day of that time limit`
    AND NOT (    `the action has been started`
             AND `the day the action was started` `is no later than` `the last day of that time limit`)

§§ `Division 6 -- s 52 defendants, s 55F costs, s 57 limitation`

DECLARE `Defendant answer` IS ONE OF
    `against the insured person and the insurer as joint defendants (s 52(1))`
    `against the insurer alone, or the insured person and the insurer jointly (s 52(2))`

-- s 52(1): "the action must be brought against the insured person and the insurer as joint defendants." (2):
-- "However, an action may be brought against the insurer alone if-- (a) the insured person can not be identified; or
-- (b) the insured person is dead or it is impracticable to serve the insured person."
GIVEN `the insured person can be identified`                     IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insured person is dead or impracticable to serve`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Defendant answer`
`the s 52 answer` `the insured person can be identified` `the insured person is dead or impracticable to serve` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the insured person can be identified`) OR `the insured person is dead or impracticable to serve`
    THEN `against the insurer alone, or the insured person and the insurer jointly (s 52(2))`
    ELSE `against the insured person and the insurer as joint defendants (s 52(1))`

DECLARE `Costs answer` IS ONE OF
    `s 55F does not apply: the award is more than the upper offer limit`
    `no costs are to be awarded (s 55F(2)(a))`
    `costs to the claimant on an indemnity basis from the day proceedings started, none before (s 55F(2)(b))`
    `costs to the insurer on a standard basis from the day proceedings started, none before (s 55F(2)(c))`
    `costs to the claimant on a standard basis up to the declared costs limit (s 55F(3)(a))`
    `costs to the claimant on a standard basis up to the declared costs limit before proceedings started, and on an indemnity basis after (s 55F(3)(b))`
    `costs to the claimant on a standard basis up to the declared costs limit before proceedings started; to the insurer on a standard basis after (s 55F(3)(c))`

-- s 55F(1): applies "if a court awards an amount equal to the upper offer limit or less in damages" (not to appellate
-- costs). (2): an award "equal to the lower offer limit or less": (a) less than the claimant's mandatory final offer
-- but more than the insurer's: no costs; (b) equal to or more than the claimant's offer: costs to the claimant on an
-- indemnity basis from the day proceedings started; (c) equal to or less than the insurer's offer: costs to the
-- insurer on a standard basis from that day. (3): an award more than the lower offer limit but not more than the upper:
-- (a) between the offers: claimant, standard basis up to the declared costs limit; (b) at or above the claimant's
-- offer: claimant, standard to the limit before, indemnity after; (c) at or below the insurer's offer: claimant,
-- standard to the limit before; insurer, standard after.
-- The limits are fixed by the Minister under s 100A and asked as facts. The paragraphs are tested in their order, so
-- where the claimant's offer is at or below the insurer's and the award lies between them, (b) is taken (finding 10).
-- s 55F(4)-(7) (costs for procedural failure, repetition, late investigations, later offers) are left to the court.
GIVEN `the damages awarded`              IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant's mandatory final offer` IS A NUMBER
      `the insurer's mandatory final offer`  IS A NUMBER
      `the lower offer limit`            IS A NUMBER
      `the upper offer limit`            IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Costs answer`
`the s 55F answer` `the damages awarded` `the claimant's mandatory final offer` `the insurer's mandatory final offer` `the lower offer limit` `the upper offer limit` MEANS
    IF `the damages awarded` GREATER THAN `the upper offer limit`
    THEN `s 55F does not apply: the award is more than the upper offer limit`
    ELSE IF `the damages awarded` AT MOST `the lower offer limit`
         THEN IF `between the offers`
              THEN `no costs are to be awarded (s 55F(2)(a))`
              ELSE IF `at or above the claimant's offer`
                   THEN `costs to the claimant on an indemnity basis from the day proceedings started, none before (s 55F(2)(b))`
                   ELSE `costs to the insurer on a standard basis from the day proceedings started, none before (s 55F(2)(c))`
         ELSE IF `between the offers`
              THEN `costs to the claimant on a standard basis up to the declared costs limit (s 55F(3)(a))`
              ELSE IF `at or above the claimant's offer`
                   THEN `costs to the claimant on a standard basis up to the declared costs limit before proceedings started, and on an indemnity basis after (s 55F(3)(b))`
                   ELSE `costs to the claimant on a standard basis up to the declared costs limit before proceedings started; to the insurer on a standard basis after (s 55F(3)(c))`
    WHERE
        `between the offers` MEANS
                `the damages awarded` LESS THAN `the claimant's mandatory final offer`
            AND `the damages awarded` GREATER THAN `the insurer's mandatory final offer`
        `at or above the claimant's offer` MEANS
            `the damages awarded` AT LEAST `the claimant's mandatory final offer`

DECLARE `Limitation answer` IS ONE OF
    `the period of limitation has not ended`
    `s 57 lets proceedings be brought after the period of limitation, up to and including` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `s 57 lets proceedings be brought within the longer period the court allows (s 57(2)(b))`
    `s 57 does not help: notice was not given before the period of limitation ended`
    `s 57 does not help: the 6 months after notice have ended and the court has allowed no longer period`

-- s 57(1): "If notice of a claim is given under division 3 ... before the end of the period of limitation applying to
-- the claim, the claimant may bring a proceeding in court based on the claim even though the period of limitation has
-- ended." (2): "However, the proceeding may only be brought after the end of the period of limitation if it is brought
-- within-- (a) 6 months after the notice is given or leave to bring the proceeding is granted; or (b) a longer period
-- allowed by the court." (5): a period extended under part 3 of the Limitation of Actions Act 1974 counts as extended.
-- The leave route of s 57(1)-(2) is out of scope (NOTES.md). The period of limitation is a fact.
-- READING: "before the end" includes the last day of the period.
GIVEN `the last day of the period of limitation` IS A DATE
      `notice has been given`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day notice was given`                 IS A DATE
      `the court allowed a longer period`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of bringing the proceeding`       IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Limitation answer`
`the s 57 answer` `the last day of the period of limitation` `notice has been given` `the day notice was given` `the court allowed a longer period` `the day of bringing the proceeding` MEANS
    IF `the day of bringing the proceeding` `is no later than` `the last day of the period of limitation`
    THEN `the period of limitation has not ended`
    ELSE IF NOT (`notice has been given` AND `the day notice was given` `is no later than` `the last day of the period of limitation`)
         THEN `s 57 does not help: notice was not given before the period of limitation ended`
         ELSE IF `the court allowed a longer period`
              THEN `s 57 lets proceedings be brought within the longer period the court allows (s 57(2)(b))`
              ELSE IF `the day of bringing the proceeding` `is no later than` `six months after notice`
                   THEN `s 57 lets proceedings be brought after the period of limitation, up to and including` `six months after notice`
                   ELSE `s 57 does not help: the 6 months after notice have ended and the court has allowed no longer period`
    WHERE
        `six months after notice` MEANS `the day` 6 `months after` `the day notice was given`

§§ `Regulative rules`

-- Clock: days. Each rule's day 0 is the day that starts it, named in its comment.
DECLARE `MAI party` IS ONE OF
    `the claimant`
    `the insurer`
    `the supervising principal`

DECLARE `MAI act` IS ONE OF
    `give notice of the claim`
    `give notice of the claim with a reasonable excuse for the delay`
    `give the additional information form`
    `give written notice responding to the notice of claim`
    `give written notice admitting or denying liability`
    `respond in writing to the offer`
    `start proceedings`
    `refund all fees and costs`
    `respond to the request for information`

-- s 37(2)-(3). Day 0: the day of the accident (or, under s 40, the day the minority or incapacity ended). Within the
-- s 37(2) period notice is owed. After it "the obligation to give the notice continues" with a reasonable excuse; for a
-- vehicle that cannot be identified it ends in the bar at 9 months. The stable l4 starts the LEST rule at the first
-- event or WAITUNTIL after the deadline, so the cases WAITUNTIL the day after the period, and the second window is
-- counted from that day. For an identified vehicle s 37(3) sets no end, and the rule waits.
GIVEN `days in the s 37(2) period`                                IS A NUMBER
      `the vehicle can be identified`                             IS A BOOLEAN
      `days from the day after the period to the end of the 9 months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `MAI party` `MAI act`
DECIDE `s 37 -- the claimant must give notice of the claim within the period, and after it with a reasonable excuse` IS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    MUST  `give notice of the claim`
    WITHIN `days in the s 37(2) period`
    LEST  `the continuing obligation`
    WHERE
        `the continuing obligation` MEANS
            IF `the vehicle can be identified`
            THEN PARTY `the claimant`
                 MUST  `give notice of the claim with a reasonable excuse for the delay`
            ELSE PARTY `the claimant`
                 MUST  `give notice of the claim with a reasonable excuse for the delay`
                 WITHIN `days from the day after the period to the end of the 9 months`
                 LEST  BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 37(3): notice was not given to the Nominal Defendant within 9 months after the motor vehicle accident, so the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred"

-- s 37A(3). Day 0: the day of the insurer's request. The court may order the claimant to remedy a default (s 50(1)).
GIVEN `days in the month after the request` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `MAI party` `MAI act`
DECIDE `s 37A -- the claimant must give the additional information form within 1 month after the request` IS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    MUST  `give the additional information form`
    WITHIN `days in the month after the request`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 37A(3): the additional information form was not given within 1 month after the request; the court may order the claimant to remedy the default (s 50(1))"

-- s 39(1)(a), (3). Day 0: the day the insurer received the notice.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `MAI party` `MAI act`
DECIDE `s 39 -- the insurer must respond to the notice of claim within 14 days` IS
    PARTY `the insurer`
    MUST  `give written notice responding to the notice of claim`
    WITHIN 14
    LEST  BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "s 39(3): the insurer did not respond within 14 days after receiving the notice, and is conclusively presumed satisfied that the notice was given as required"

-- s 41(1). Day 0: the day the insurer received (or under s 41(3) is taken to receive) the notice. The court may order
-- the insurer to remedy a default (s 50(2)).
GIVEN `days in the 6 months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `MAI party` `MAI act`
DECIDE `s 41 -- the insurer must say whether it admits or denies liability within 6 months` IS
    PARTY `the insurer`
    MUST  `give written notice admitting or denying liability`
    WITHIN `days in the 6 months`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "s 41(1): the insurer did not give written notice of whether liability is admitted or denied within 6 months after receiving notice of the claim; the court may order it to remedy the default (s 50(2))"

-- s 41(5), the claimant's side. Day 0: the day the claimant received the insurer's offer.
GIVEN `days in the 3 months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `MAI party` `MAI act`
DECIDE `s 41(5) -- the claimant must respond to a written offer of settlement within 3 months` IS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    MUST  `respond in writing to the offer`
    WITHIN `days in the 3 months`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 41(5): no written response accepting or rejecting the offer within 3 months after receiving it; the court may order the claimant to remedy the default (s 50(1))"

-- s 45(2)(b). Day 0: the day the claimant received the insurer's request.
GIVEN `days in the month after the request` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `MAI party` `MAI act`
DECIDE `s 45 -- the claimant must respond to the insurer's request for information within 1 month` IS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    MUST  `respond to the request for information`
    WITHIN `days in the month after the request`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 45(2)(b): the claimant did not respond to the insurer's request within 1 month after receiving it; the court may order the claimant to remedy the default (s 50(1))"

-- s 51C(6). Day 0: the day the mandatory final offers were exchanged. Proceedings must not be started while the
-- offers remain open, for 14 days.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `MAI party` `MAI act`
DECIDE `s 51C(6) -- the claimant must not start proceedings while a mandatory final offer remains open` IS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    SHANT `start proceedings`
    WITHIN 14
    LEST  BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 51C(6): proceedings must not be started while a mandatory final offer remains open (14 days)"

-- s 51D(1), (4)-(5). Day 0: the day the compulsory conference concluded. The 60 days are what the action "should" meet:
-- missing them is no breach (s 51D(4)), and the claimant may still start; if the court then fixes a time limit on the
-- insurer's application, missing that bars the claim (s 51D(5)). Starting is the claimant's choice, so it is a DO rule.
-- The court-fixed limit is counted, like the s 37 rule's second window, from the first event after the 60 days.
GIVEN `days the claimant should start within`      IS A NUMBER
      `the court fixed a time limit`               IS A BOOLEAN
      `days in the court's time limit`             IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `MAI party` `MAI act`
DECIDE `s 51D -- the claimant should start the action within 60 days, and must within any limit the court fixes` IS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    DO    `start proceedings`
    WITHIN `days the claimant should start within`
    LEST  `after the 60 days`
    WHERE
        `after the 60 days` MEANS
            IF `the court fixed a time limit`
            THEN PARTY `the claimant`
                 MUST  `start proceedings`
                 WITHIN `days in the court's time limit`
                 LEST  BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 51D(5): the action was not started within the time limit the court fixed under s 51D(4)(b), so the claim is barred"
            ELSE PARTY `the claimant`
                 MAY   `start proceedings`

-- s 37AA(2). Day 0: the day the claimant terminated the engagement.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `MAI party` `MAI act`
DECIDE `s 37AA -- the supervising principal must refund all fees and costs within 14 days after the termination` IS
    PARTY `the supervising principal`
    MUST  `refund all fees and costs`
    WITHIN 14
    LEST  BREACH BY `the supervising principal` BECAUSE "s 37AA(2): fees and costs, including disbursements, were not refunded within 14 days after the termination"

-- The rules' numbers from dates.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Notice facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in the s 37(2) period for` `the facts` MEANS
    `the days from` (`the start of a period under s 40` `the facts` (`the facts`'s `the day of the accident`)) `to` (`the last day of the s 37(2) period` `the facts`)

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Notice facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days after the s 37(2) period to the bar for` `the facts` MEANS
    (`the days from` `day 0` `to` (`the last day before the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred` `the facts`))
    MINUS (`the days in the s 37(2) period for` `the facts`)
    MINUS 1
    WHERE
        `day 0` MEANS `the start of a period under s 40` `the facts` (`the facts`'s `the day of the accident`)

GIVEN `n`       IS A NUMBER
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in` `n` `months from` `the day` MEANS
    `the days from` `the day` `to` (`the day` `n` `months after` `the day`)
